          "title": "Overview",
          "descriptions": [],
          "contents": [
            {
              "type": "formatted-text",
              "segments": [
                {
                  "text": "On May 21, 2026, American Fork "
                },
                {
                  "format": "link",
                  "text": "Officer Bronson T. Kitchen",
                  "url": {
                    "$ref": "entity-officer-page-bronson-t-kitchen",
                    "$path": [
                      "url"
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": " stopped Aaron Booker on I-15 near Farmington for a suspected HOV-lane violation."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "formatted-text",
              "segments": [
                {
                  "text": "When Booker declined to lower his partially open window further, Kitchen threatened to call the highway patrol to break it. Kitchen’s own incident report acknowledges that his statement escalated the encounter. He ultimately released Booker with a verbal warning and no citation."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "formatted-text",
              "segments": [
                {
                  "text": "Booker later challenged the basis for the stop and the accuracy of Kitchen’s report. In public comments to the American Fork City Council, he said Kitchen apologized after footage of the encounter went viral, but that the report contained false statements. Booker called for accountability and announced his intention to pursue a civil-rights lawsuit."
                }
              ]
            },
